{"data": [{"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-25T00:16:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114149166360170507"], "id": "2114149166360170507", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 26, "impression_count": 129835, "like_count": 219, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 22, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Man this is so bleak", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2114149166360170507"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-25T00:00:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114144942096572731"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 27, "start": 20, "tag": "hookem"}]}, "id": "2114144942096572731", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14479, "like_count": 22, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Texas with the lead #hookem", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2114144942096572731"}, {"author_id": "30034124", "created_at": "2026-10-24T22:04:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114115720929780219"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Time is something with which we have tremendous experience, but a d...", "display_url": "youtu.be/20KMDzbXzr8?si…", "end": 189, "expanded_url": "https://youtu.be/20KMDzbXzr8?si=7ZJ-P0PsaVeBI79A", "images": [{"height": 720, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114115725535199232/JR46k7bI?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114115725535199232/JR46k7bI?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 166, "status": 200, "title": "What is time?", "unwound_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?si=7ZJ-P0PsaVeBI79A&v=20KMDzbXzr8&feature=youtu.be", "url": "https://t.co/m3dpHXUor6"}]}, "id": "2114115720929780219", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 8, "impression_count": 5089, "like_count": 60, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 9}, "text": "Time is something with which we have tremendous experience, but a detailed and scientific definition of time and how it works eludes even the most educated of minds.\nhttps://t.co/m3dpHXUor6", "url": "https://x.com/Fermilab/status/2114115720929780219"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-24T20:53:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114098005934780817"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 58, "start": 52, "tag": "China"}], "urls": [{"description": "Mr. Kim was said to have crossed the border via a newly opened bridge for his first visit to China in over a year, as the countries move to deepen ties.", "display_url": "nytimes.com/2026/10/24/wor…", "end": 255, "expanded_url": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/24/world/asia/north-korea-kim-jong-un-china.html", "images": [{"height": 1687, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113960009889443840/HKwZQoZ3?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 3000}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113960009889443840/HKwZQoZ3?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 232, "status": 200, "title": "North Korea’s Kim Jong-un Arrives in China, South Korea Says", "unwound_url": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/24/world/asia/north-korea-kim-jong-un-china.html", "url": "https://t.co/01wTRtv5Jp"}]}, "id": "2114098005934780817", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1797, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"North Korea leader Kim Jong-un visited neighboring #China on Saturday in his 1st visit there in more than a year, meeting w/a senior official &amp; declaring gratitude for Beijing’s decades of support, according to 🇨🇳 state media\"\nhttps://t.co/01wTRtv5Jp", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2114098005934780817"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-24T20:49:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114096984223093218"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 7, "start": 1, "tag": "China"}], "urls": [{"description": "China's ruling Communist Party announced key personnel changes in six provinces on Saturday, two days before it holds a closed-door conclave in Beijing ​from October 26 to 29.", "display_url": "reuters.com/world/china/ch…", "end": 274, "expanded_url": "https://www.reuters.com/world/china/chinas-communist-party-names-new-provincial-chiefs-ahead-fifth-plenum-2026-10-24/", "images": [{"height": 1005, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113971942026014720/z4JaNO3L?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1920}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113971942026014720/z4JaNO3L?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 251, "status": 200, "title": "China's Communist Party names new provincial chiefs ahead of fifth plenum", "unwound_url": "https://www.reuters.com/world/china/chinas-communist-party-names-new-provincial-chiefs-ahead-fifth-plenum-2026-10-24/", "url": "https://t.co/NC3Z2xaI30"}]}, "id": "2114096984223093218", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1806, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "\"#China's ruling Communist Party announced key personnel changes in 6 provinces on Saturday, including 2 new provincial party chiefs &amp; ​6 officials positioned to become governors, before it holds a closed-door conclave in Beijing ‌from Oct 26-29\"\nhttps://t.co/NC3Z2xaI30", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2114096984223093218"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-24T20:32:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114092644913623197"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 32, "id": "17974586", "start": 20, "username": "willystaley"}, {"end": 43, "id": "1542228578", "start": 35, "username": "JDVance"}]}, "id": "2114092644913623197", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 122, "impression_count": 76681, "like_count": 525, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 44, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "I’m on day 4 of the @willystaley / @JDVance diet of nothing but meat and fermented vegetables and I have to say I’ve been feeling great. My brain got rewired so fast. Basically the only thing I crave anymore is kimchi.", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2114092644913623197"}, {"author_id": "423769635", "created_at": "2026-10-24T18:17:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114058648905302115"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 115, "id": "180556387", "start": 103, "username": "bcaresearch"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/b2ZNdpPceF", "end": 139, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2114058648905302115/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114058617359843328", "start": 116, "url": "https://t.co/b2ZNdpPceF"}]}, "id": "2114058648905302115", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 8538, "like_count": 34, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "US government interest expenses are among the highest in the developed world relative to GDP.\n\nSource: @bcaresearch https://t.co/b2ZNdpPceF", "url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2114058648905302115"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-24T17:49:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114051637245587714"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/E9vs2jkeHz", "end": 266, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2114051637245587714/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114051631159324672", "start": 243, "url": "https://t.co/E9vs2jkeHz"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/E9vs2jkeHz", "end": 266, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2114051637245587714/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114051631121580032", "start": 243, "url": "https://t.co/E9vs2jkeHz"}, {"display_url": "x.com/neil_irwin/sta…", "end": 290, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/neil_irwin/status/2113668825766043779", "start": 267, "url": "https://t.co/tD1v45X4Qp"}]}, "id": "2114051637245587714", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1832, "impression_count": 468153, "like_count": 2853, "quote_count": 48, "reply_count": 147, "retweet_count": 173}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113668825766043779", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "We obviously haven’t had the major jobs wipeout yet. But you read stuff like this. And you read what economics students themselves are saying about working with AI (ht @odavis_h) and it’s hard not to feel like the seismic shift is on its way. https://t.co/E9vs2jkeHz https://t.co/tD1v45X4Qp", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2114051637245587714"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-24T17:17:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114043703987716533"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "China's cabinet, the ​State Council, urged government agencies to effectively ‌mitigate job displacement caused by artificial intelligence applications, according to guidelines issued on Friday on ​AI and employment.", "display_url": "reuters.com/business/world…", "end": 87, "expanded_url": "https://www.reuters.com/business/world-at-work/china-urges-government-agencies-mitigate-ai-job-displacement-2026-10-23/", "images": [{"height": 1005, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113622059033231360/D5vAVzeq?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1920}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113622059033231360/D5vAVzeq?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 64, "status": 200, "title": "China urges government agencies to mitigate AI job displacement", "unwound_url": "https://www.reuters.com/business/world-at-work/china-urges-government-agencies-mitigate-ai-job-displacement-2026-10-23/", "url": "https://t.co/5K2G3nfGYf"}]}, "id": "2114043703987716533", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1738, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "China urges government agencies to mitigate AI job displacement\nhttps://t.co/5K2G3nfGYf", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2114043703987716533"}, {"author_id": "1327359720", "created_at": "2026-10-24T16:22:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114029845823004932"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Torsten Slok, chief economist at Apollo, discusses risks related to delays in data center construction, calling the AI buildout “a very, very critical driver of growth at the moment” for the US economy. He speaks on “Bloomberg Surveillance.” (Source: Bloomberg)", "display_url": "bloomberg.com/news/articles/…", "end": 262, "expanded_url": "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-10-22/ai-buildout-becoming-economic-predictor-economist-slok-video", "images": [{"height": 675, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114029847232356352/OFdG8f5T?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114029847232356352/OFdG8f5T?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 239, "status": 200, "title": "AI Buildout Becoming an Economic Predictor, Says Economist Slok", "unwound_url": "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-10-22/ai-buildout-becoming-economic-predictor-economist-slok-video", "url": "https://t.co/qbmBTSVxN1"}]}, "id": "2114029845823004932", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 40, "impression_count": 17994, "like_count": 205, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 24, "retweet_count": 39}, "text": "Credit spreads on all things AI are widening out enough to slow some AI projects: Apollo’s Torsten Slok. “Rates are maybe not important for AI but yields are important for AI:” Slok. “Credit markets are beginning to vote with their feet.” https://t.co/qbmBTSVxN1", "url": "https://x.com/lisaabramowicz1/status/2114029845823004932"}, {"author_id": "423769635", "created_at": "2026-10-24T15:57:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114023381410705508"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 159, "id": "1652717271469506565", "start": 148, "username": "BoringBiz_"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/OqLIn8Cth7", "end": 183, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2114023381410705508/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114023283075031040", "start": 160, "url": "https://t.co/OqLIn8Cth7"}]}, "id": "2114023381410705508", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 8, "impression_count": 6996, "like_count": 25, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "Anthropic is estimated to generate more quarterly revenue than established corporate giants including Intel, Uber, Coca-Cola, and Netflix.\n\nSource: @BoringBiz_ https://t.co/OqLIn8Cth7", "url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2114023381410705508"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-10-24T15:39:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114018834206376063"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/ShortCircuit_K…", "end": 266, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/ShortCircuit_KJ/status/2113710774837301561", "start": 243, "url": "https://t.co/Jx3QpGjoRL"}]}, "id": "2114018834206376063", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 43, "impression_count": 13545, "like_count": 62, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 3}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113710774837301561", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "same dynamic played out with Agencies in the US before the global financial crisis.  Treasury issuance lagged the growth in dollar fx reserves in a big way, forcing a range of investors to in effect treat Agencies as a safe assets ....  \n\n1/2 https://t.co/Jx3QpGjoRL", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2114018834206376063"}, {"author_id": "423769635", "created_at": "2026-10-24T14:41:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114004283368804420"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 114, "id": "1652541", "start": 106, "username": "Reuters"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/EjhhbOHR5R", "end": 138, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2114004283368804420/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114004270244605952", "start": 115, "url": "https://t.co/EjhhbOHR5R"}]}, "id": "2114004283368804420", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 13, "impression_count": 7426, "like_count": 29, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "France has the OECD’s second-highest ratio of public pension spending to GDP, behind only Italy.\n\nSource: @Reuters https://t.co/EjhhbOHR5R", "url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2114004283368804420"}, {"author_id": "1327359720", "created_at": "2026-10-24T14:33:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114002437367312423"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Harvard economist Jason Furman's new vibe-coded site offers a glimpse of what's possible for AI-produced economic analysis.", "display_url": "axios.com/2026/10/23/ai-…", "end": 261, "expanded_url": "https://www.axios.com/2026/10/23/ai-economic-research-analysis", "images": [{"height": 768, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113668824385880064/wsuoEVYX?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1366}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113668824385880064/wsuoEVYX?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 238, "status": 200, "title": "AI economic research is getting really good", "unwound_url": "https://www.axios.com/2026/10/23/ai-economic-research-analysis", "url": "https://t.co/nfqsDAngQP"}]}, "id": "2114002437367312423", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 96, "impression_count": 44212, "like_count": 261, "quote_count": 9, "reply_count": 26, "retweet_count": 56}, "text": "Jason Furman on AI vs human economists: If he were running the CEA today and had a choice between 20 highly qualified staff members “versus the AI systems that we have today, I would somewhat regretfully and sadly choose the AI systems.” https://t.co/nfqsDAngQP", "url": "https://x.com/lisaabramowicz1/status/2114002437367312423"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-10-24T09:34:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113927127036985651"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/World_Data_A/s…", "end": 277, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/World_Data_A/status/2113582190592180729", "start": 254, "url": "https://t.co/HrTrKiirMj"}]}, "id": "2113927127036985651", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 55, "impression_count": 25826, "like_count": 237, "quote_count": 7, "reply_count": 20, "retweet_count": 34}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113582190592180729", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Amazing how many folks still haven't figured out that the tariffs have led Chinese goods (China increasingly exports high value components) to take a one stop flight rather than a non stop flight to the US -- the bilateral data doesn't tell us much\n\n1/2 https://t.co/HrTrKiirMj", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2113927127036985651"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-24T04:44:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113854194272669707"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 103, "start": 100, "tag": "AI"}], "urls": [{"description": "Major Chinese AI developers DeepSeek and MiniMax have won state approval ​for global use of their AI ‌models, according to a post on Thursday on a social media account affiliated with ​state broadcaster CCTV.", "display_url": "reuters.com/business/media…", "end": 155, "expanded_url": "https://www.reuters.com/business/media-telecom/chinas-deepseek-minimax-win-approval-ai-global-use-state-media-affiliated-entity-2026-10-23/", "images": [{"height": 1005, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113538730438823936/sipFLoZf?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1920}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113538730438823936/sipFLoZf?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 132, "status": 200, "title": "China's DeepSeek, MiniMax win approval for AI global use, state media-affiliated entity says", "unwound_url": "https://www.reuters.com/business/media-telecom/chinas-deepseek-minimax-win-approval-ai-global-use-state-media-affiliated-entity-2026-10-23/", "url": "https://t.co/TY05dStruB"}]}, "id": "2113854194272669707", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 1987, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "\"Major Chinese AI developers DeepSeek &amp; MiniMax have won state approval for global use of their #AI ‌models, according to CCTV\" https://t.co/TY05dStruB", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2113854194272669707"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-24T03:10:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113830411830735332"], "id": "2113830411830735332", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 58, "impression_count": 65140, "like_count": 1170, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 35, "retweet_count": 11}, "text": "The Sopranos ep. where Christopher takes an acting class is fascinating. It’s the only time where the viewer stops and thinks “Wow, Imperioli is an incredible actor.” But the thought only pops into your head right then, because you forget he’s acting during the rest of the show.", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2113830411830735332"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-10-23T23:59:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113782458927714319"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/allisonpapson/…", "end": 28, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/allisonpapson/status/2113772077425541457", "start": 5, "url": "https://t.co/P77tgIjU1z"}]}, "id": "2113782458927714319", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5941, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113772077425541457", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "NCRC https://t.co/P77tgIjU1z", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2113782458927714319"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-23T23:58:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113782032018923712"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/jimibarkway/st…", "end": 203, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/jimibarkway/status/2113780213528092804", "start": 180, "url": "https://t.co/nVtJD4Tzh7"}]}, "id": "2113782032018923712", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 11, "impression_count": 18554, "like_count": 61, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113780213528092804", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Tbh idk. But if Dario’s fear is misaligned ASI, then what’s so good about holding back Fable, or coming up with more aggressive bio classifiers? These things seem like a sideshow. https://t.co/nVtJD4Tzh7", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2113782032018923712"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-23T23:41:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113777940072894778"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/_nathancalvin/…", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/_nathancalvin/status/2113273917544505798", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/sp4Xiuj63x"}]}, "id": "2113777940072894778", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 53, "impression_count": 27138, "like_count": 245, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 20, "retweet_count": 13}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113273917544505798", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Good post here from Nathan. Sure, Anthropic has taken actions that may have cost it money. But in Dario’s post, there’s a conspicuous absence of any actual pacing or slowing progress towards RSI, despite a widespread view that “alignment” is nowhere close to being solved. https://t.co/sp4Xiuj63x", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2113777940072894778"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-23T23:14:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113770962130981071"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "General public budget revenue slipped 0.1% in September, while land-sale receipts plunged 23.2%, adding to pressure on local government finances", "display_url": "caixinglobal.com/2026-10-24/chi…", "end": 37, "expanded_url": "https://www.caixinglobal.com/2026-10-24/chinas-fiscal-revenue-slips-as-land-sale-slump-deepens-102496694.html", "images": [{"height": 373, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113770971979190272/t3UcBS7p?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 560}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113770971979190272/t3UcBS7p?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 14, "status": 200, "title": "China’s Fiscal Revenue Slips as Land-Sale Slump Deepens", "unwound_url": "https://www.caixinglobal.com/2026-10